ST NOT be claimed as executed. Distinguish in every handoff\nbetween (a) observed, (b) inferred, and (c) unverified.\nRationale: fabricated or assumed test results poison later phases; evidence\nis the only transferable state between phases.\n\n### IV. Simple, Scoped Implementations\nPrefer the smallest implementation that satisfies the stated requirements\nwithin the declared scope (for milestone 1: `src/cachetools/tagged.py` and\nits own tests). Reuse existing components (for example, `cachetools.LRUCache`\nfor bounded storage) instead of reimplementing them. No new dependencies,\nno speculative features, no refactoring of unrelated code. Any added\ncomplexity MUST be justified in writing against a stated requirement.\nRationale: scope creep and gratuitous complexity are the main failure modes\nof autonomous implementation; reuse also reduces regression risk on the\npreserved public API.\n"}